1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,733
Welcome to Unit Three of Algebra One:
linear inequalities.

2
00:00:04,183 --> 00:00:09,379
An inequality compares two sides using
less than or greater than. In this lesson,

3
00:00:09,379 --> 00:00:13,741
we'll solve inequalities and graph their
solutions on a number line.

4
00:00:14,867 --> 00:00:19,860
There are four symbols: less than, greater
than, less than or equal to, and greater

5
00:00:19,860 --> 00:00:20,883
than or equal to.

6
00:00:21,333 --> 00:00:26,225
x is greater than two means x can be any
number bigger than two, like three, two

7
00:00:26,225 --> 00:00:27,754
and a half, or a million.

8
00:00:28,900 --> 00:00:33,896
To graph x greater than two, put an open
circle at two, because two itself is not

9
00:00:33,896 --> 00:00:37,412
included. Then shade to the right, toward
bigger numbers.

10
00:00:37,862 --> 00:00:42,827
For x less than or equal to negative one,
use a closed circle at negative one,

11
00:00:42,827 --> 00:00:45,755
because it is included, and shade to the
left.

12
00:00:46,900 --> 00:00:52,339
Solving an inequality works just like
solving an equation. Take x plus four is

13
00:00:52,339 --> 00:00:53,385
less than nine.

14
00:00:53,835 --> 00:00:57,227
Subtract four from both sides, and x is
less than five.

15
00:00:58,367 --> 00:01:03,657
Now a two-step example: three x minus five
is greater than or equal to seven.

16
00:01:04,107 --> 00:01:08,395
Add five to both sides: three x is greater
than or equal to twelve.

17
00:01:08,845 --> 00:01:13,730
Divide by three: x is greater than or
equal to four. Closed circle at four,

18
00:01:13,730 --> 00:01:14,968
shade to the right.

19
00:01:16,100 --> 00:01:21,681
To check, pick a number in the shaded
region, like five. Three times five, minus

20
00:01:21,681 --> 00:01:24,889
five, is ten, and ten is at least seven.
True.

21
00:01:25,339 --> 00:01:29,656
A number outside, like zero, gives
negative five, which is not at least

22
00:01:29,656 --> 00:01:31,419
seven. So the graph is right.

23
00:01:32,567 --> 00:01:36,321
Your turn. Solve and graph two x plus one
is less than seven.

24
00:01:36,771 --> 00:01:38,222
Pause the video and try it.

25
00:01:38,672 --> 00:01:44,275
Subtract one: two x is less than six.
Divide by two: x is less than three. Open

26
00:01:44,275 --> 00:01:46,757
circle at three, shade to the left.

27
00:01:47,900 --> 00:01:51,868
Let's solve an inequality with variables
on both sides and graph it.

28
00:01:53,300 --> 00:01:59,046
Solve two times the quantity x plus three,
minus five, is less than or equal to four

29
00:01:59,046 --> 00:02:01,577
x minus nine, and graph the solution.

30
00:02:02,700 --> 00:02:05,665
Distribute the two: two x plus six minus
five.

31
00:02:06,800 --> 00:02:09,701
Combine like terms on the left: two x plus
one.

32
00:02:10,833 --> 00:02:16,696
Subtract two x from both sides, so the x
term stays positive. One is less than or

33
00:02:16,696 --> 00:02:18,577
equal to two x minus nine.

34
00:02:19,700 --> 00:02:23,561
Add nine to both sides: ten is less than
or equal to two x.

35
00:02:24,700 --> 00:02:30,872
Divide by two: five is less than or equal
to x. Reading from x's side, x is greater

36
00:02:30,872 --> 00:02:32,508
than or equal to five.

37
00:02:33,633 --> 00:02:39,010
The solution is x greater than or equal to
five. On the number line, put a closed dot

38
00:02:39,010 --> 00:02:42,679
at five, because five is included, and
shade to the right.

39
00:02:43,800 --> 00:02:49,012
Watch out. Five less than or equal to x is
the same as x greater than or equal to

40
00:02:49,012 --> 00:02:54,031
five, so read it from x's side before
graphing. Less than or equal and greater

41
00:02:54,031 --> 00:02:59,500
than or equal use a closed dot. And test a
point in the shaded region and one outside

42
00:02:59,500 --> 00:02:59,693
it.

43
00:03:00,833 --> 00:03:06,272
Your turn. Solve three times the quantity
x minus two, plus four, is greater than

44
00:03:06,272 --> 00:03:09,495
five x minus twelve. Pause the video and
try it.

45
00:03:14,033 --> 00:03:20,140
Simplify to three x minus two is greater
than five x minus twelve. Subtract three x

46
00:03:20,140 --> 00:03:26,320
and add twelve: ten is greater than two x,
so x is less than five. Open dot at five,

47
00:03:26,320 --> 00:03:27,644
shade to the left.

48
00:03:28,766 --> 00:03:31,454
Inequalities have one rule that equations
don't.

49
00:03:31,904 --> 00:03:37,049
When you multiply or divide both sides by
a negative number, you must flip the

50
00:03:37,049 --> 00:03:39,093
inequality sign. Let's see why.

51
00:03:40,233 --> 00:03:43,049
Start with a true statement: two is less
than five.

52
00:03:43,499 --> 00:03:48,853
Multiply both sides by negative one, and
you get negative two and negative five.

53
00:03:49,303 --> 00:03:54,616
On the number line, negative two is to the
right of negative five, so negative two is

54
00:03:54,616 --> 00:03:59,117
greater than negative five. The order
reversed, so the sign has to flip.

55
00:04:00,266 --> 00:04:02,847
Solve negative three x is less than
twelve.

56
00:04:03,297 --> 00:04:08,907
Divide both sides by negative three, and
flip the sign. x is greater than negative

57
00:04:08,907 --> 00:04:09,249
four.

58
00:04:10,399 --> 00:04:14,666
Another one: five minus two x is greater
than or equal to eleven.

59
00:04:15,116 --> 00:04:19,297
Subtract five: negative two x is greater
than or equal to six.

60
00:04:19,747 --> 00:04:25,398
Divide by negative two and flip: x is less
than or equal to negative three. Closed

61
00:04:25,398 --> 00:04:28,430
circle at negative three, shade to the
left.

62
00:04:29,566 --> 00:04:34,195
Careful: the sign flips only when you
multiply or divide by a negative.

63
00:04:34,645 --> 00:04:39,968
In four x is greater than negative eight,
you divide by positive four, so the sign

64
00:04:39,968 --> 00:04:45,291
stays the same. x is greater than negative
two. The negative eight doesn't matter.

65
00:04:46,433 --> 00:04:51,937
Now variables on both sides: two x plus
three is less than five x minus nine.

66
00:04:52,387 --> 00:04:57,357
Subtract five x: negative three x plus
three is less than negative nine.

67
00:04:57,807 --> 00:05:03,351
Subtract three: negative three x is less
than negative twelve. Divide by negative

68
00:05:03,351 --> 00:05:06,021
three and flip: x is greater than four.

69
00:05:07,166 --> 00:05:11,475
Your turn. Solve negative four x plus two
is greater than fourteen.

70
00:05:11,925 --> 00:05:13,376
Pause the video and try it.

71
00:05:13,826 --> 00:05:19,379
Subtract two: negative four x is greater
than twelve. Divide by negative four and

72
00:05:19,379 --> 00:05:21,847
flip: x is less than negative three.

73
00:05:22,966 --> 00:05:26,721
Here's a worked example where you have to
flip the inequality sign.

74
00:05:28,166 --> 00:05:31,451
Solve seven minus x over three is less
than nine.

75
00:05:32,599 --> 00:05:37,314
Subtract seven from both sides. Negative x
over three is less than two.

76
00:05:38,433 --> 00:05:42,102
To get x alone, multiply both sides by
negative three.

77
00:05:43,233 --> 00:05:48,145
Because we multiplied by a negative
number, the inequality flips. Less than

78
00:05:48,145 --> 00:05:51,617
becomes greater than. x is greater than
negative six.

79
00:05:52,766 --> 00:05:58,049
The solution is x greater than negative
six. Open dot at negative six, shade to

80
00:05:58,049 --> 00:05:58,718
the right.

81
00:05:59,866 --> 00:06:05,208
Watch out. Flip the sign only when you
multiply or divide by a negative number.

82
00:06:05,208 --> 00:06:10,617
Adding or subtracting never flips it.
Testing a point is the best way to catch a

83
00:06:10,617 --> 00:06:11,429
missed flip.

84
00:06:12,566 --> 00:06:17,686
Your turn. Solve four minus two x is
greater than or equal to three x plus

85
00:06:17,686 --> 00:06:20,246
nineteen. Pause the video and try it.

86
00:06:24,766 --> 00:06:30,311
Subtract three x and four: negative five x
is greater than or equal to fifteen.

87
00:06:30,311 --> 00:06:35,646
Divide by negative five and flip: x is
less than or equal to negative three.

88
00:06:36,766 --> 00:06:41,265
A compound inequality joins two
inequalities with the word and, or the

89
00:06:41,265 --> 00:06:41,779
word or.

90
00:06:42,229 --> 00:06:44,960
In this lesson, we'll solve and graph both
kinds.

91
00:06:46,099 --> 00:06:51,460
And means both must be true at once. x is
greater than negative two, and x is less

92
00:06:51,460 --> 00:06:52,179
than three.

93
00:06:52,629 --> 00:06:56,981
The solution is the overlap: all the
numbers between negative two and three.

94
00:06:57,431 --> 00:07:02,218
We often write it as one statement:
negative two is less than x, which is less

95
00:07:02,218 --> 00:07:02,893
than three.

96
00:07:04,033 --> 00:07:09,091
To solve negative one is less than or
equal to two x plus three, which is less

97
00:07:09,091 --> 00:07:12,203
than nine, do the same thing to all three
parts.

98
00:07:12,653 --> 00:07:18,115
Subtract three: negative four is less than
or equal to two x, which is less than six.

99
00:07:18,565 --> 00:07:23,791
Divide by two: negative two is less than
or equal to x, which is less than three.

100
00:07:24,933 --> 00:07:30,526
Or means at least one must be true. x is
less than negative one, or x is greater

101
00:07:30,526 --> 00:07:31,994
than or equal to two.

102
00:07:32,444 --> 00:07:35,409
The graph has two pieces pointing away
from each other.

103
00:07:36,533 --> 00:07:42,527
To solve an or inequality, solve each part
separately. x plus four is less than two,

104
00:07:42,527 --> 00:07:44,810
or three x is greater than nine.

105
00:07:45,260 --> 00:07:50,232
The first part gives x less than negative
two. The second gives x greater than

106
00:07:50,232 --> 00:07:50,615
three.

107
00:07:51,733 --> 00:07:56,277
A quick summary: and gives the overlap,
usually a segment between two numbers.

108
00:07:56,727 --> 00:08:00,695
Or gives both pieces together, usually two
rays pointing outward.

109
00:08:01,833 --> 00:08:07,148
Your turn. Solve negative five is less
than three x plus one, which is less than

110
00:08:07,148 --> 00:08:08,211
or equal to ten.

111
00:08:08,661 --> 00:08:10,112
Pause the video and try it.

112
00:08:10,562 --> 00:08:16,005
Subtract one: negative six is less than
three x, which is at most nine. Divide by

113
00:08:16,005 --> 00:08:19,970
three: negative two is less than x, which
is at most three.

114
00:08:21,100 --> 00:08:25,303
Let's solve a compound inequality written
as one three-part statement.

115
00:08:26,733 --> 00:08:32,017
Solve negative five is less than or equal
to the quantity two x minus one, over

116
00:08:32,017 --> 00:08:34,157
three, which is less than three.

117
00:08:35,300 --> 00:08:39,865
Whatever you do, do it to all three parts.
Multiply every part by three.

118
00:08:41,000 --> 00:08:42,451
Add one to all three parts.

119
00:08:43,600 --> 00:08:48,657
Divide every part by two. x is between
negative seven and five, including

120
00:08:48,657 --> 00:08:50,597
negative seven but not five.

121
00:08:51,733 --> 00:08:57,386
So x is from negative seven, included, up
to five, not included. Closed dot at

122
00:08:57,386 --> 00:09:00,864
negative seven, open dot at five, shade
between.

123
00:09:02,000 --> 00:09:07,072
Watch out. Do the same operation to all
three parts at once. Keep track of each

124
00:09:07,072 --> 00:09:12,015
symbol: closed dot for less than or equal,
open dot for less than. And an and

125
00:09:12,015 --> 00:09:15,611
inequality like this one is shaded between
the two dots.

126
00:09:16,733 --> 00:09:22,102
Your turn. Solve negative one is less than
three minus two x, which is less than or

127
00:09:22,102 --> 00:09:24,819
equal to nine. Pause the video and try it.

128
00:09:29,367 --> 00:09:34,785
Subtract three: negative four is less than
negative two x, which is at most six.

129
00:09:34,785 --> 00:09:40,136
Divide by negative two and flip both
signs: x is from negative three, included,

130
00:09:40,136 --> 00:09:41,761
up to two, not included.

131
00:09:42,900 --> 00:09:45,311
Absolute value means distance from zero.

132
00:09:45,761 --> 00:09:49,899
In this lesson, we'll solve equations that
contain absolute values.

133
00:09:51,033 --> 00:09:56,628
The absolute value of five is five, and
the absolute value of negative five is

134
00:09:56,628 --> 00:10:00,143
also five. Both numbers are five units
from zero.

135
00:10:00,593 --> 00:10:05,926
So if the absolute value of x equals five,
x can be five or negative five.

136
00:10:07,067 --> 00:10:10,245
Here's the method. First, isolate the
absolute value.

137
00:10:10,695 --> 00:10:16,168
Then split into two equations: the inside
equals the positive number, or the inside

138
00:10:16,168 --> 00:10:17,949
equals the negative number.

139
00:10:19,067 --> 00:10:22,608
Solve the absolute value of x minus three
equals seven.

140
00:10:23,058 --> 00:10:26,663
Split it. x minus three equals seven, so x
equals ten.

141
00:10:27,113 --> 00:10:33,060
Or x minus three equals negative seven, so
x equals negative four. Both answers are

142
00:10:33,060 --> 00:10:34,708
seven units from three.

143
00:10:35,833 --> 00:10:41,465
Now solve two times the absolute value of
x plus one, plus four, equals twelve.

144
00:10:41,915 --> 00:10:47,347
Subtract four: two times the absolute
value equals eight. Divide by two: the

145
00:10:47,347 --> 00:10:50,278
absolute value of x plus one equals four.

146
00:10:50,728 --> 00:10:56,425
So x plus one is four or negative four,
which gives x equals three or x equals

147
00:10:56,425 --> 00:10:57,448
negative five.

148
00:10:58,567 --> 00:11:03,928
Watch out: the absolute value of x plus
two equals negative three has no solution,

149
00:11:03,928 --> 00:11:06,609
because a distance can never be negative.

150
00:11:07,059 --> 00:11:11,411
And if an absolute value equals zero,
there is exactly one solution.

151
00:11:12,533 --> 00:11:17,035
Your turn. Solve the absolute value of two
x minus one equals nine.

152
00:11:17,485 --> 00:11:18,935
Pause the video and try it.

153
00:11:19,385 --> 00:11:25,839
Two x minus one equals nine, so x equals
five. Or two x minus one equals negative

154
00:11:25,839 --> 00:11:28,388
nine, so x equals negative four.

155
00:11:29,533 --> 00:11:34,578
Here's a worked absolute value equation
where you must isolate the absolute value

156
00:11:34,578 --> 00:11:34,952
first.

157
00:11:36,400 --> 00:11:42,211
Solve three times the absolute value of
two x minus five, plus four, equals twenty

158
00:11:42,211 --> 00:11:42,565
five.

159
00:11:43,700 --> 00:11:46,836
First isolate the absolute value. Subtract
four.

160
00:11:47,966 --> 00:11:52,702
Divide by three. The absolute value of two
x minus five equals seven.

161
00:11:53,833 --> 00:11:57,268
Now split. The inside is either seven or
negative seven.

162
00:11:58,400 --> 00:11:59,978
Add five in both cases.

163
00:12:01,100 --> 00:12:04,961
Divide by two. x equals six or x equals
negative one.

164
00:12:06,100 --> 00:12:08,745
There are two solutions: six and negative
one.

165
00:12:09,866 --> 00:12:14,549
Watch out. Isolate the absolute value
before you split into two cases. If the

166
00:12:14,549 --> 00:12:19,535
absolute value equals a negative number,
there's no solution at all. And there are

167
00:12:19,535 --> 00:12:21,664
usually two answers, so check both.

168
00:12:22,800 --> 00:12:28,393
Your turn. Solve two times the absolute
value of x plus three, minus five, equals

169
00:12:28,393 --> 00:12:30,672
nine. Pause the video and try it.

170
00:12:35,200 --> 00:12:41,294
Add five and divide by two: the absolute
value of x plus three is seven. So x plus

171
00:12:41,294 --> 00:12:46,570
three is seven or negative seven, giving x
equals four or negative ten.

172
00:12:47,700 --> 00:12:52,777
In this last lesson of Unit Three, we'll
combine absolute value with inequalities.

173
00:12:53,900 --> 00:12:59,140
The absolute value of x is less than three
means x is less than three units from

174
00:12:59,140 --> 00:12:59,468
zero.

175
00:12:59,918 --> 00:13:04,721
That's every number between negative three
and three. So it becomes an and

176
00:13:04,721 --> 00:13:09,134
inequality: negative three is less than x,
which is less than three.

177
00:13:10,267 --> 00:13:15,372
The absolute value of x is greater than
three means x is more than three units

178
00:13:15,372 --> 00:13:16,027
from zero.

179
00:13:16,477 --> 00:13:22,117
That's two pieces: x is less than negative
three, or x is greater than three. So it

180
00:13:22,117 --> 00:13:23,815
becomes an or inequality.

181
00:13:24,933 --> 00:13:29,755
Solve the absolute value of x minus two is
less than or equal to five.

182
00:13:30,205 --> 00:13:34,642
Write negative five is at most x minus
two, which is at most five.

183
00:13:35,092 --> 00:13:40,212
Add two to all three parts: negative three
is at most x, which is at most seven.

184
00:13:41,333 --> 00:13:45,536
Solve the absolute value of two x plus one
is greater than seven.

185
00:13:45,986 --> 00:13:50,875
Split it: two x plus one is less than
negative seven, or two x plus one is

186
00:13:50,875 --> 00:13:52,130
greater than seven.

187
00:13:52,580 --> 00:13:56,420
So x is less than negative four, or x is
greater than three.

188
00:13:57,567 --> 00:14:01,556
Here's a memory trick. Less than becomes
and: one segment in the middle.

189
00:14:02,006 --> 00:14:07,467
Greater than becomes or: two rays pointing
outward. And always isolate the absolute

190
00:14:07,467 --> 00:14:08,257
value first.

191
00:14:09,400 --> 00:14:13,731
Your turn. Solve the absolute value of x
plus one is less than four.

192
00:14:14,181 --> 00:14:15,631
Pause the video and try it.

193
00:14:16,081 --> 00:14:21,296
Negative four is less than x plus one,
which is less than four. Subtract one:

194
00:14:21,296 --> 00:14:25,020
negative five is less than x, which is
less than three.

195
00:14:26,166 --> 00:14:31,307
Let's solve an absolute value inequality
and see why it becomes an or statement.

196
00:14:32,733 --> 00:14:37,682
Solve the absolute value of three x plus
one, minus two, is greater than eight.

197
00:14:38,799 --> 00:14:44,572
Isolate the absolute value by adding two.
The absolute value of three x plus one is

198
00:14:44,572 --> 00:14:45,754
greater than ten.

199
00:14:46,899 --> 00:14:52,393
Greater than means the inside is more than
ten units from zero, in either direction.

200
00:14:52,393 --> 00:14:53,897
That's an or statement.

201
00:14:55,033 --> 00:14:56,590
Subtract one in both parts.

202
00:14:57,733 --> 00:15:03,279
Divide by three. x is greater than three,
or x is less than negative eleven thirds.

203
00:15:04,399 --> 00:15:09,456
The solution is x less than negative
eleven thirds, or x greater than three.

204
00:15:09,456 --> 00:15:12,250
Two open dots, with shading going outward.

205
00:15:13,399 --> 00:15:18,075
Watch out. Absolute value greater than a
number gives an or, shaded outward.

206
00:15:18,075 --> 00:15:23,120
Absolute value less than a number gives an
and, shaded between. And when you write

207
00:15:23,120 --> 00:15:25,581
the negative case, flip that inequality.

208
00:15:26,699 --> 00:15:32,199
Your turn. Solve the absolute value of two
x minus three is less than or equal to

209
00:15:32,199 --> 00:15:34,507
seven. Pause the video and try it.

210
00:15:39,033 --> 00:15:44,565
Less than gives an and: negative seven to
seven. Add three and divide by two: x is

211
00:15:44,565 --> 00:15:47,331
from negative two to five, both included.

212
00:15:48,466 --> 00:15:53,250
Let's finish Unit Three with a realistic
problem that uses inequalities and

213
00:15:53,250 --> 00:15:54,781
absolute value together.

214
00:15:56,199 --> 00:16:00,617
A factory makes bolts that should be forty
millimeters long. A bolt passes if its

215
00:16:00,617 --> 00:16:04,543
length is within zero point six
millimeters of forty. Write and solve an

216
00:16:04,543 --> 00:16:08,851
absolute value inequality for passing
lengths. Then, if each passing bolt earns

217
00:16:08,851 --> 00:16:13,214
twenty five cents profit, how many must
pass to earn at least one hundred eighty

218
00:16:13,214 --> 00:16:13,650
dollars?

219
00:16:14,799 --> 00:16:20,637
Within zero point six of forty means the
distance between L and forty is at most

220
00:16:20,637 --> 00:16:26,547
zero point six. That's the absolute value
